discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** `fs.readFile` runs concurrently with `fs.lstat` via `Promise.all`, creating a TOCTOU window — a symlinked `SKILL.md` targeting `/dev/zero` would start an unbounded read before `lstat` rejects it, OOMing the process. The codebase's established convention (`O_NOFOLLOW` in `gitDiff.ts:93`, `gitUtils.ts:22`, `sessionStorageUtils.ts:20`) closes exactly this class.

Failure scenario: attacker commits `.qwen/skills/auto-skill-foo/SKILL.md` as a symlink to `/dev/zero` (git mode `120000`, survives clone). Next curator scan calls `readManagedSkill` → `Promise.all([lstat, lstat, readFile])` → `readFile` follows the symlink and reads null bytes until V8's heap limit is hit.

```suggestion
  const directoryStat = await fs.lstat(directoryPath);
  const manifestStat = await fs.lstat(manifestPath);
  if (
    directoryStat.isSymbolicLink() || !directoryStat.isDirectory() ||
    manifestStat.isSymbolicLink() || !manifestStat.isFile()
  ) {
    return undefined;
  }
  const content = await fs.readFile(manifestPath, 'utf8');
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

`fs.readFile` 通过 `Promise.all` 与 `fs.lstat` 并发执行，产生 TOCTOU 窗口——指向 `/dev/zero` 的符号链接 `SKILL.md` 会在 `lstat` 拒绝之前开始无限读取，导致进程 OOM。代码库已有的惯例（`gitDiff.ts:93`、`gitUtils.ts:22` 等处使用 `O_NOFOLLOW`）正是为了闭合此类问题。

</details>

_— qwen3.7-max via Qwen Code /review_

